In my games I observed that there is quite some span in the amount of
moves necessary to ascend. The first dozen ascensions were mostly 80000
moves with little variance (+/- 100!), later it changed to a range from
50000 to 130000 (ignoring an extinctionist). The difference in moves
was an effect correlated with, e.g., whether there was an unattended
altar or coaligned altar until the castle, whether I had chosen to get
teleportitis, and similar things which have a great impact on the speed
to proceed. If implemented, any new timing effect would have to give a
significant effect in the above moves range (otherwise it would be quite
useless, I suppose we agree), but since they are (in the two examples)
based on luck (generated altars), or punish (still more than currently)
some gameplay (deliberate teleportitis), that's what I wouldn't like.

So if you'd couple the effect on the specific kill rate of a species
you are free to escape a fight with no penalties.[*]

